    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d528">

                <pb facs="0473" n="463" xml:id="pg463"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.001 Chiang Kai-shek/7–2849: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Taipei</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Macdonald</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Taipei</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-07-28T16:00:00+09:00">July 28, 1949—4 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 28—1:02 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>325. Reliably informed that Generalissimo will remain Taiwan only 1 week [to]
                    complete organization new offices here, then proceed Chungking and Lanchow.
                    Quirino [and] he may go Korea for Far East Union Conference middle August. New
                    signatories to pact may subscribe only to principles or to one or more material
                    commitments depending on each nation’s desire.</p>
                <p>Repeated Canton 137.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Macdonald</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
